  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through Sunday)\nIssued at 155 PM CDT Mon Sep 28 2026\n\nBy Wednesday, the base of the upper-level trough moves over our area \nand a Pacific front begins pushing through the region. As these \nsystems progress, shower/storm chances move east across the eastern \nhalf of our CWA and bring drier conditions out west. However, it \nshould be noted that dry slotting may prevent some areas from seeing \nsome rain (including the Midland/Odessa area). Nevertheless, flash \nflooding due to locally heavy rainfall will be possible across the \neastern Permian Basin and Lower Trans-Pecos. Behind the Pacific \nfront, southwesterly breezy conditions are forecast before subsiding \nWednesday evening. Model guidance shows the front pushing south and \neast by the latter half of the week, keeping shower/storm chances \nacross our far eastern zones (though adjustments to the forecasts \nare likely). Aside from rain chances, a cooling trend is expected to \nlast all week (thanks to the front), with highs possibly dropping \ninto the 70s by the end of the week and into the weekend.\n  \nGreening",
